  "timing_notes": "Alternating warmed wall-time trials on the same physical cells. Fortran uses separately compiled original arithmetic with O2, no fast-math/LTO, and runtime checks disabled. Timed iteration capture is off; its conditional branch remains. Fortran includes copying fixed number/volume/environment/geometry, setting species properties and the explicit solubility mask, and copying physical outputs. Startup, I/O, iteration diagnostics and checksums are excluded. Checked and optimized outputs and iteration counts are first verified identical outside timing. The timed JAX wrapper returns only core and wet diameter, leaving its iteration counter unused for compilation to eliminate; exact counts are validated in a separate untimed call. JAX includes dispatch plus synchronization of both outputs, excluding transfer and compilation. Fortran loops over cells/bins; JAX batches them and retains masked bins until the slowest active iteration converges. Thread settings are recorded, not normalized. Neither path advances a trajectory across timing repetitions. These measurements are CPU process timings, not full-model or GPU performance."
